2016,"Type":"IC50","comparison":{"compound_id":"OBMD011700","measurement_id":"MCTM-038151","value":"56 ± 15","numeric":56}}],"logp":[{"abbreviation_in_the_article":8,"value":1.84,"value_relation":"=","type_authors":"logP","method":"shake-flask","aqueous_phase":"water","doi":"10.1002/ejic.201600857","year":2016,"record_id":"MLDB-002052","detection":"ICP-MS","method_description":"By using the shake-flask method, log P values of complexes 5–8 were obtained similarly to other sparingly soluble metal complexes, as described elsewhere.30 Briefly, the saturated solution of each compound in water (presaturated with n-octanol) was prepared by agitating in an ultrasonic bath. The supernatant was filtered through a 0.45 µm membrane filter and shaken with an equal volume of water-saturated n-octanol for 2 h with a mechanical shaker. Platinum concentrations in the aqueous phase after phase separation (Caq.) and in the initial saturated solution (C0) were determined by ICP-MS. Partition coefficients were calculated from the equation: log P = log[(C₀ - Caq) / Caq]"}]}